  "tep_assessment": "TEP does not modify exterior luminosity measurements. The conformal factor A ~ 1 in the exterior where TDE emission escapes, so TDE luminosities are unaffected by TEP. The temporal-freeze mechanism only operates inside the horizon, where photons cannot escape to reach the observer. The observed sub-Eddington TDEs are therefore not explained by TEP; they reflect known astrophysical effects (super-Eddington winds, reprocessing, viewing angle, circularization efficiency).",
